    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold`) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the GOLD membership tier with minimal structural impact:\n\n- **New isolated helper** `HouseholdTier.applyGold(...)` (`rest/function/owner/HouseholdTier.java`) \u2014 counts owners sharing the same `householdId` and, when the household has 3+ members, overrides the DTO's tier to `GOLD`. It runs *after* the mapper's base tier, so GOLD takes precedence and the existing BRONZE/SILVER rules apply otherwise. Owners with no household are left untouched.\n- **Two one-line delegations** in the responders `RespondWithOwner` and `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, so both the create response and later reads reflect GOLD.\n\nI deliberately kept the logic out of the large `Owner` entity and out of the MapStruct mapper (which has no repository access). The whole counting logic lives in a fresh class with zero surrounding complexity, and each existing responder gains a single call \u2014 cyclomatic complexity of the edited methods is unchanged. No persistent schema change was needed since the household size is recomputed from the shared `householdId` at response time.",
